ic shared memory so the block's output threads reuse them instead of repeatedly fetching those source fields from global memory. The sequential pairwise arithmetic and one-output-per-active-thread strategy remain close to baseline; barriers and shared-memory occupancy costs may offset the reduced global loads, so this is a performance hypothesis for measurement.", "transformations": "{"files":["src/nbody_kernel.cu"],"retained":["Stage source x, y, z, and mass in four 256-element shared-memory arrays, loading each tile cooperatively.","Synchronize after tile loads and after tile consumption so all output lanes, including tail-block lanes, safely participate before shared storage is reused.","Keep the source-particle accumulation in ascending tile/source order and guard output work and writes with i < n."]}", "applicability": "", "next_experiment": "", "evidence_ids": []}, "source_available": true, "details_are_bounded": true}, {"id": "fcfebc51a67f48d7", "kind": "experiment", "role": "T2", "tree_id": "e1:T2", "mission_id": "fcfebc51a67f48d7", "facts": {"commit": "f63c9b81df70aac6a75035827434cbdb26a3afac", "base_commit": "22138f39a9036399442f78956289de1c33a07b3d", "parent_id": null, "source_ids": [], "source_count": 0}, "measured_outcome": {"status": "valid", "correct": true, "mean_seconds": 0.002745536300643952, "score": 0.40261046959044094}, "diagnostic": "", "model_interpretation": {"claim": "Giving each thread two outputs lets it load each source particle's position and mass once and reuse those values for both targets. Mapping the targets to threadIdx.x and threadIdx.x + blockDim.x preserves contiguous lane accesses for each output group. This may reduce repeated source loads, while the additional target state and accumulators may increase register pressure; official measurements are needed to assess the tradeoff.", "transformations": "{"files":["src/launch.json","src/nbody_kernel.cu"],"retained":["Assign two output particles per thread, with the second target at first + blockDim.x so each target group remains contiguous across lanes.","Stream each source particle's position and mass once per thread and reuse the values for both target force calculations.","Maintain separate target states and force accumulators; guard the second target for partial groups and write each valid output once.","Set items_per_block to 512 while retaining block=256 and shared_memory_bytes=0."]}", "applicability": "", "next_experiment": "", "evidence_ids": []}, "source_available": true, "details_are_bounded": true}, {"id": "253c00e28c904a54", "kind": "experiment", "role": "T3", "tree_id": "e1:T3", "mission_id": "253c00e28c904a54", "facts": {"commit": "7148961870199c9bcce2304b698d6b995bada423", "base_commit": "22138f39a9036399442f78956289de1c33a07b3d", "parent_id": null, "source_ids": [], "source_count": 0}, "measured_outcome": {"status": "incorrect", "correct": false, "mean_seconds": null, "score": 0.0}, "diagnostic": "Protected correctness checks failed", "model_interpretation": {"claim": "With the same per-thread mapping, global-memory accesses, rsqrtf, and target-mass cancellation, forming (G * neighbor_mass * invDist) and (invDist * invDist) independently may shorten the dependent multiplication chain for each pair. This is a performance hypothesis; the changed float32 rounding must pass the independent oracle.", "transformations": "{"files":["src/nbody_kernel.cu"],"retained":["Keep one output per thread, the pairwise global-memory strategy, explicit rsqrtf, G=1, softening, update order, and the self-interaction skip.","Reorder the reciprocal-cube multiplications so the neighbor-mass/invDist product and invDist-squared product can be formed independently before their final multiplication."]}", "applicability": "", "next_experiment": "", "evidence_ids": []}, "source_available": true, "details_are_bounded": true}, {"id": "42ddd5d53dc94097", "kind": "experiment", "role": "T4", "tree_id": "e1:T4", "mission_id": "42ddd5d53dc94097", "facts": {"commit"